  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "start",
      "name": "Start",
      "doc": "Flow: D03 ¶76–77. Trigger: record action 'Open Allocation' on NSSOL Projects, passing projectInfo (D03 ¶254, D06 ¶174)."
    },
    {
      "id": "allocationMainScreenMerge",
      "type": "xor",
      "name": "Before Allocation Main Screen",
      "doc": "SYNTHESIZED: not a documented node. 3 flows reach 'Allocation Main Screen'; this converging exclusive gateway merges them."
    },
    {
      "id": "allocationMainScreen",
      "type": "userTask",
      "name": "Allocation Main Screen",
      "doc": "Interface: NSSOL_SEC_Allocation (D04 ¶168–237). Flow: D03 ¶80–91. Inputs: rule inputs at D04 ¶174–184. PROPOSAL (AL-7): outputs are the flags the buttons set (D03 ¶88–91) and the lists D04 ¶179–180 describe as passed back to PV. No documented assignee (AL-1).",
      "inputs": [
        "projectInfo",
        "selectedEmployees",
        "selectedSubcontractors",
        "assignedEmployees",
        "assignedSubcontractors",
        "isAddEmployee",
        "isAddSubcontractor",
        "isAssign",
        "allocationCancel"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "assignedEmployees",
        "assignedSubcontractors",
        "isAddEmployee",
        "isAddSubcontractor",
        "isAssign",
        "allocationCancel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "allocationMainScreenGateway",
      "type": "xor",
      "name": "After Allocation Main Screen",
      "doc": "SYNTHESIZED: not a documented node. The branches at D03 ¶93–115 leave 'Allocation Main Screen' directly; this exclusive gateway carries their conditions."
    },
    {
      "id": "end1",
      "type": "end",
      "name": "End",
      "doc": "Flow: D03 ¶93."
    },
    {
      "id": "employeeSearchScreen",
      "type": "userTask",
      "name": "Employee Search Screen",
      "doc": "Interface: NSSOL_GRID_Employee_Search_Screen (D04 ¶241–251). Flow: D03 ¶98–101. PROPOSAL (AL-7): outputs from D03 ¶101–102. D04 lists no rule inputs for this interface; D06 ¶182 says process variables are passed to it as ri! without naming them, so no inputs are bound (AL-12).",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        "selectedEmployees",
        "empCancel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "subcontractorSearchScreen",
      "type": "userTask",
      "name": "Subcontractor Search Screen",
      "doc": "Interface: NSSOL_GRID_Subcontractor_Search_Screen (D04 ¶255–265). Flow: D03 ¶108–111. PROPOSAL (AL-7): outputs from D03 ¶111–112. D04 lists no rule inputs for this interface; D06 ¶183 says process variables are passed to it as ri! without naming them, so no inputs are bound (AL-12).",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        "selectedSubcontractors",
        "SubconCancel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "allocationConfirmation",
      "type": "userTask",
      "name": "Allocation Confirmation",
      "doc": "Interface: NSSOL_FRM_Allocation_Confirmation (D04 ¶83–97). Flow: D03 ¶118–121. Inputs: rule inputs at D04 ¶89–91. AL-C3 CONFLICT: D04 ¶96 says Submit saves the assigned lists to the process variables, but the form's only rule input is projectInfo (D04 ¶89–91) and D06 ¶184 calls it a read-only summary; no outputs are bound until this is resolved. AL-C2 CONFLICT: D04 ¶97 documents a Back button; the diagram has no path back.",
      "inputs": [
        "projectInfo"
      ],
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "writeMapEmployeeRecords",
      "type": "serviceTask",
      "name": "Write Map Employee Records",
      "doc": "Flow: D03 ¶124–126. AL-4: untyped in the diagram; MapEmployeeStore is a proposed test double. Saves assignedEmployees to NSSOL Map Employees (D03 ¶125); the documented record contents are in AL-9.",
      "service": {
        "class": "nssol.service.MapEmployeeStore",
        "operation": "save"
      },
      "inputs": [
        "assignedEmployees"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "assignedEmployees"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "writeMapSubcontractorRecords",
      "type": "serviceTask",
      "name": "Write Map Subcontractor Records",
      "doc": "Flow: D03 ¶129–130. AL-4: untyped in the diagram; MapSubcontractorStore is a proposed test double. Saves assignedSubcontractors to NSSOL Map Subcontractors (D03 ¶130); record contents are not documented (AL-9).",
      "service": {
        "class": "nssol.service.MapSubcontractorStore",
        "operation": "save"
      },
      "inputs": [
        "assignedSubcontractors"
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "assignedSubcontractors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "end2",
      "type": "end",
      "name": "End",
      "doc": "Flow: D03 ¶133."
    }
  ],
  "flows": [
    {
      "from": "start",
      "to": "allocationMainScreenMerge"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreen",
      "to": "allocationMainScreenGateway"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreenGateway",
      "to": "end1",
      "name": "allocationCancel = true",
      "condition": "return allocationCancel != null && allocationCancel;"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreenGateway",
      "to": "employeeSearchScreen",
      "name": "isAddEmployee = true",
      "condition": "return isAddEmployee != null && isAddEmployee;"
    },
    {
      "from": "employeeSearchScreen",
      "to": "allocationMainScreenMerge",
      "name": "empCancel = true / confirm"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreenGateway",
      "to": "subcontractorSearchScreen",
      "name": "isAddSubcontractor = true",
      "condition": "return isAddSubcontractor != null && isAddSubcontractor;"
    },
    {
      "from": "subcontractorSearchScreen",
      "to": "allocationMainScreenMerge",
      "name": "SubconCancel = true / confirm"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreenGateway",
      "to": "allocationConfirmation",
      "name": "isAssign = true",
      "condition": "return isAssign != null && isAssign;"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationConfirmation",
      "to": "writeMapEmployeeRecords"
    },
    {
      "from": "writeMapEmployeeRecords",
      "to": "writeMapSubcontractorRecords"
    },
    {
      "from": "writeMapSubcontractorRecords",
      "to": "end2"
    },
    {
      "from": "allocationMainScreenMerge",
      "to": "allocationMainScreen"
    }
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "cancel_writesNothing",
      "start": {
        "projectInfo": {
          "projectId": 3,
          "projectName": "Test Tower Construction",
          "isActive": true
        }
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "task": "allocationMainScreen",
          "complete": {
            "allocationCancel": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "status": "COMPLETED",
        "saves": {
          "MapEmployeeStore": 0,
          "MapSubcontractorStore": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "assign_savesEmployeesAndSubcontractors",
      "start": {
        "projectInfo": {
          "projectId": 3,
          "projectName": "Test Tower Construction",
          "isActive": true
        }
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "task": "allocationMainScreen",
          "complete": {
            "isAssign": true,
            "assignedEmployees": [
              {
                "employeeMappedId": 1,
                "projectId": 3,
                "employeeId": 10,
                "role": "Site Manager"
              }
            ],
            "assignedSubcontractors": [
              {
                "subconMappedId": 1,
                "projectId": 3,
                "subconId": 20,
                "companyName": "Acme Subcontracting"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "task": "allocationConfirmation",
          "complete": {}
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "status": "COMPLETED",
        "saves": {
          "MapEmployeeStore": 1,
          "MapSubcontractorStore": 1
        },
        "savedLists": {
          "MapEmployeeStore": 1,
          "MapSubcontractorStore": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "addEmployee_returnsToMainScreenThenCancels",
      "start": {
        "projectInfo": {
          "projectId": 3,
          "projectName": "Test Tower Construction",
          "isActive": true
        }
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "task": "allocationMainScreen",
          "complete": {
            "isAddEmployee": true
          }
        },
        {
          "task": "employeeSearchScreen",
          "complete": {
            "selectedEmployees": [
              {
                "empId": 10,
                "empName": "Test Employee"
              }
            ],
            "empCancel": false
          }
        },
        {
          "task": "allocationMainScreen",
          "complete": {
            "allocationCancel": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "status": "COMPLETED",
        "saves": {
          "MapEmployeeStore": 0,
          "MapSubcontractorStore": 0
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "AL-1",
      "text": "No task assignee/candidate group documented; the four user tasks are left unassigned (same gap as SR-3)."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-2",
      "text": "Branch precedence and default are undocumented (D03 ¶93–115): nothing says which flag wins if several are true, or what happens if none is. All four flags default to null (D03 ¶66–69). Conditions are emitted in document order with no default flow."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-3",
      "text": "Flag reset on loop-back is undocumented (D03 ¶102–103, ¶112–113): nothing clears isAddEmployee / isAddSubcontractor when a search screen returns, so the same branch is taken again unless the form resets the flag."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-4",
      "text": "The two write nodes carry no task type in the diagram (D03 ¶124, ¶129); modelled as service tasks. MapEmployeeStore and MapSubcontractorStore are proposed test doubles (same gap as SR-4)."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-C1",
      "text": "CONFLICT: D03 ¶220 counts 3 forms (allocation + 2 search); the flow diagram has a fourth user task, Allocation Confirmation (D03 ¶118–119). Model follows the diagram."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-C2",
      "text": "CONFLICT: D04 ¶97 gives Allocation Confirmation a Back button returning to the allocation screen; the flow diagram shows no path back from it (D03 ¶118–124). Model follows the diagram: no back flow."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-C3",
      "text": "CONFLICT: D04 ¶96 says the Allocation Confirmation Submit button saves the assigned employee/subcontractor lists to the process variables; its only rule input is projectInfo (D04 ¶89–91) and D06 ¶184 describes it as a read-only summary. The main screen already passes both lists back (D04 ¶179–180). No outputs are bound on the confirmation task."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-C4",
      "text": "CONFLICT (start permissions; same as C3 in the Register Project packet): D03 ¶242 says the process models are open to all authenticated users; D07 ¶96 says NP Users cannot start instances, while D07 ¶98 makes record-action security the gate and D07 ¶115 lets NP Users see Allocate. Not modelled."
    },
    {
      "id": "AL-C5",
      "text": "CONFLICT (form, not flow): the allocation colour boundary at exactly 70% is green in D02 ¶179–180 and orange in D02 ¶292–293 and D04 ¶231–232; red is #E64345 in D02 ¶178 and #FF0000 in D04 ¶230. Not modelled."
    },
